{
  "name": "Error Collector (global)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ec-sticky",
      "name": "READ ME",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -280,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "## Global error collector\n\nFires whenever ANY workflow that names this one as its Error Workflow fails, and writes one row to `n8n_errors`. It sends NOTHING in the moment -- `Daily Error Digest` mails the summary at 08:00.\n\nSet it per workflow: three dots -> Settings -> **Error Workflow** -> `Error Collector (global)`. Worth setting on every workflow.\n\nDeliberately NOT routed through here: `Telegram - Alta 1a1 Fallida` in subscription-lifecycle. A paying athlete stuck without access is worth interrupting for; a transient API error is not.\n\nUses the Postgres **Insert** operation, not Execute Query -- `queryReplacement` splits its input on commas, and error messages are full of commas."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ec-trigger",
      "name": "Error Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "ec-insert",
      "name": "Store Error in Postgres",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        240,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "schema": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "public",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "table": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "n8n_errors",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "workflow_name": "={{ $json.workflow?.name || '' }}",
            "workflow_id": "={{ $json.workflow?.id || '' }}",
            "node_name": "={{ $json.execution?.lastNodeExecuted || '' }}",
            "error_message": "={{ $json.execution?.error?.message || '' }}",
            "execution_id": "={{ $json.execution?.id || '' }}",
            "execution_url": "={{ $json.execution?.url || '' }}"
          }
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Members Postgres"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Error Trigger": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Store Error in Postgres",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "active": false,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "pinData": {},
  "tags": []
}